<title>FRANCE: Seita to ask buy-back permission.</title>
<headline>Seita to ask buy-back permission.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seita chairman Jean-Dominique Comolli said he would ask shareholders for authorisation to buy-back up to 15 percent of the share capital for a period of five years.</p>
<p>The proposal will be made to the annual general meeting of May 20.</p>
<p>Seita said the move was to allow shareholders the benefit of its important cash reserves, which were 6.3 billion francs at the end of 1996.</p>
</text>
